# will_detour — thinking, a will takes a way a step longer than its shortest, within three acts
#
# Lockpicking is a will: its lock is the Test Door off the yard. From the Test Field its shortest way is
# two acts (walk to the yard, unlock). The Field–Rock Track is no step of that way — it goes past the
# yard to the rock — but from the rock the yard is one walk, so through the track the lock is three acts
# off (follow the track, walk to the yard, unlock): within Config.Narrative.WillMaxPathSteps. Thinking
# with lockpicking on the track therefore proposes following it, where it once refused it as "not on
# the way". Observing is unchanged: the plan is still the two-act way.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm lockpicking --grant-item hairpin --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Field–Rock Track"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

advance 12 180
expect-state will "will lockpicking steps=2"

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose lockpicking
advance 12 180
regions
expect-not but that does nothing for it

strategy succeed
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Rock
expect-verb follow_path
quit
